PATCH 548: `word == -1` is a constant false -- nine in-mission handlers never ran.

DGROUP:0x6da2 is the mission teardown countdown: 0xffff means NO teardown pending (armed that way at
0x47b2, `movw $0xffff,0x6da2`), and FUN_1000_a5dc raises the mission-over flag when a non-0xffff value
counts down to zero.  Ten sites in the image ask "is the mission still running?" with

    cmpw $0xffff,0x6da2

at 0x52f2, 0x535e, 0x53c5, 0x54a8, 0x5577, 0x56d1, 0x5767, 0x57f8, 0xbf3c and 0x1a5dc.

Ghidra rendered the a5dc one as `!= 0xffff` and the other NINE as `== -1`.  `DAT_2000_2da2` is
`undefined2` = `uint16_t`, which promotes to `int` under the usual arithmetic conversions, so the
compared value ranges over 0..65535 and `== -1` is a CONSTANT FALSE.  (The same expression against an
`undefined4` would be correct -- -1 converts to UINT_MAX there -- which is why the idiom is not
uniformly wrong and has to be judged per declared width.)

In each of the nine, the test is the function's FIRST statement and its body is the then-branch, so
every one of those functions was a no-op for the whole mission.  All nine are in-mission command
handlers reached through the indirect-call table (they decode `param_1 & 0x80` as the key-down bit and
toggle engine flags); the port registers each at its own address, e.g. `{0x52f2u,&FUN_0000_52f2}`.

    0000:52f2  FUN_0000_52f2
    0000:535e  FUN_0000_535e
    0000:53c5  FUN_0000_53c5
    0000:54a8  FUN_0000_54a8
    0000:5577  FUN_0000_5577
    0000:56d1  FUN_0000_56d1
    0000:5767  FUN_0000_5767
    0000:57f8  FUN_0000_57f8
    0000:bf3c  FUN_0000_bf3c

This patch changes only the constant; the comparison, the operand and the branch sense are already
what the asm says.

Seven further `undefined2 == -1` / `!= -1` sites survive elsewhere in the tree (DGROUP:0x9fd9,
0x9fd6, 0xe918, 0xe82e, 0x6db6 and two in the 0x1000 segment).  They are the same class but each
needs its own asm width and branch-sense check before it is touched, so they are NOT in this patch --
board:0017 carries them.

board:0017

